            "review_title": "Review at Oscar Saigon Weekend Buffet",
            "review_text": "KnH1993\n28 contributions\n0\nMaybe weekdays are better...\nNov 2014 • Friends\nThis place is on the 11th floor of the Oscar Hotel, so at least the view was nice, and the place is fairly clean. We bought vouchers for the lunch buffet from hotdeal.vn for $165k each (about $8 USD) and went on a Sunday. We had heard from a friend who had lunch there a while back that lunch was good but we found it to be average to below average. There weren't many dishes--maybe around 20. A few were good--their Vietnamese crepes, banh khot, banh beo and steamed clams were decent. But their other seafood dishes, like baked oysters and mussels, were cold and dry. Their pho looked pretty sad too. Dessert was fruit, a few pastries and soft serve ice cream. They didn't have a lot of the dishes that had been advertised on hotdeal, so we were disappointed. We won't be coming back.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 9, 2014",
